{"outcome":"DIRECT_SUB_OPTIMAL","best_model_id":"PGS003381","confidence":"Moderate","rationale":"Direct-match candidates for uterine cancer include exact/umbrella uterine cancer labels (PGS000541, PGS000542, PGS001795, PGS003740) and the clinically dominant subtype endometrial/uterine endometrial carcinoma (PGS000075, PGS000786, PGS002300, PGS002735-002737, PGS003381, PGS004244). Per domain knowledge, endometrial carcinoma is a strong direct match for a uterine cancer target (~90% of uterine carcinoma), so endometrial-focused models are eligible and can be preferred when better supported.

Among endometrial/uterine candidates, PGS003381 has strong endpoint fidelity (phenotyping_reported: uterine endometrial carcinoma) and favorable structural properties (lassosum, 529,365 variants) with a relatively strong reported full-model AUROC (0.761; EUR evaluation, n=144,479) compared with other endometrial candidates that are either much sparser (e.g., PGS000075/PGS000786) or show lower full-model AUROC (e.g., PGS002735-002737) or lack AUC (PGS004244). Compared to exact uterine-cancer-labeled PGS000541/PGS000542, PGS003381 shows substantially higher discrimination (full-model AUROC ~0.76 vs ~0.57), and its covariates are basic (age, top 20 PCs), making the reported metric more comparable than models with family-history and multiple epidemiologic covariates.

Main limitation: the key metric provided for PGS003381 is a full-model AUROC (and an R² reported as 0.11 without being explicitly PRS-only), so PRS-only performance is not directly observable and cannot be cleanly compared across candidates; additionally, the exact-label uterine cancer PRS from a global biobank framework (PGS001795, PRS-CS-auto) has PRS-comparable R² reported (0.001948, covariates-regressed-out) but lower AUROC (0.66) and comes from a framework context. These metric comparability constraints keep confidence below High."}

{"outcome":"DIRECT_SUB_OPTIMAL","best_model_id":"PGS000054","confidence":"Moderate","rationale":"All 5 candidates are direct matches on concept (trait_efo = late-onset Alzheimer's disease). Endpoint fidelity is strongest for PGS000053/PGS000054/PGS000334/PGS004918 which all report late-onset AD as the phenotype (PGS000053/054 explicitly familial LOAD; domain guidance treats familial late-onset forms as acceptable direct matches). PGS002289 is weaker on endpoint fidelity because phenotyping_reported is a cognition-by-age interaction phenotype rather than AD case-control status despite the same trait label.

For performance evidence, only PGS000053 and PGS000054 provide PRS-comparable effect sizes (OR per SD): 1.29 (EUR eval) vs 1.73 (AMR/Hispanic eval). Domain knowledge indicates OR per SD is a strong predictor; OR≥1.5 is strong, making PGS000054 the best-supported on visible discrimination evidence. Other candidates either report only full-model metrics (e.g., PGS004918 full-model AUROC=0.731 with unknown covariates) or an R² (PGS000334 R²=0.191) that is not clearly PRS-only and is potentially non-comparable/suspect per the heritability sanity-check guidance (and covariates are unknown).

Limitation: there is no PRS-only AUC/R² reported for PGS000054, and its evaluation ancestry is Hispanic/Latin American while several alternatives are evaluated in Europeans; without a specified deployment ancestry, this reduces certainty and keeps the outcome at sub-optimal rather than high-quality."}
